.Dd November 11, 2026
.Dt IRQ_CREATE 2
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm irq_create
.Nd create an interrupt source
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Fn irq_create root_dev kind number flags
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm creates an
.Em Irq
handle a driver can wait on with
.Xr irq_wait 2 .
.Fa root_dev
must be the
.Em RootDevice
capability with
.Dv ADMIN .
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fa kind
.Dv LEGACY (1):
.Fa number
is the ISA IRQ; the kernel translates it through the MADT interrupt-source
overrides and honours the polarity and trigger the override declares.  The
redirection entry is programmed masked and stays masked until the first
.Xr irq_wait 2
or
.Xr irq_ack 2 ;
.Fa flags
must be 0.
A GSI has one owner: a second
.Nm
for a line that is already owned fails with
.Er EBUSY ,
and closing the last handle masks the line and releases the claim.
.It Fa kind
.Dv MSI (2) or MSIX (3):
the kernel allocates a free vector from its pool of 128 vectors (0x40..0xBF)
and fills the
.Em IrqInfo
record
.Sy { vector: u32, address_lo: u32, address_hi: u32, data: u32 }
at the user pointer given in
.Fa flags .
The driver programs the returned address and data into its device's MSI
capability or MSI-X table entry; MSI and MSI-X share one encoding.
.El
The message always targets the boot processor's APIC.  For destination ids
0..255 the encoding is
.Sy address_lo = 0xFEE00000 | (id << 12)
and
.Sy address_hi = 0
in both xAPIC and x2APIC mode; the id is never placed in the upper half.
.Pp
A driver that programs the returned message must call
.Xr irq_wait 2
or
.Xr irq_ack 2
at least once before closing the handle; that marks the source live.
Closing a live MSI source without a final
.Xr irq_ack 2
quarantines its vector permanently, so a device that still points at the old
message can never reach a new
.Em Irq .
An MSI object that was never armed is treated as inert and its vector may be
reused.
The returned handle carries
.Dv READ ,
.Dv DUP
and
.Dv TRANSFER .
Closing the last legacy handle masks the source and returns the vector to
the pool.
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Er EPERM
No root capability with
.Dv ADMIN .
.It Er EINVAL
Unknown kind, invalid number, a non-zero legacy
.Fa flags ,
or a bad IrqInfo pointer.
.It Er EBUSY
The legacy GSI already has an owner.
.It Er ENOSPC
The vector pool is exhausted.
.It Er EOPNOTSUPP
The boot APIC id is above 255; the extended-destination MSI format is not
implemented.
.It Er EFAULT
The IrqInfo pointer is not writable user memory.
.It Er EMFILE
The process handle table is full.
.El
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD ABI v1.
